message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "optcurves: consecutive convexity violations of gradient-descent optimization curves"
abstract: >-
  Performance-estimation study, exact rational certificates and counterexamples, and Lean-verified theorems on
  when the optimization curve of gradient descent with constant step size can be concave at several consecutive
  steps, for L-smooth convex and strongly convex functions. For one violation and L-smooth mu-strongly convex
  functions, with step size h/L, kappa = L/mu and m = mu/L = 1/kappa, symbolic (SymPy-checked) proofs give the
  exact threshold h_1(kappa) = (1 + kappa) - sqrt((1 + kappa)^2 - (7 kappa + 1)/2) (for 0 < h < 2, no f has a
  violation exactly when h <= h_1(kappa)) and the exact worst-case violation above it,
  L h^2 max(0, -q) / (2 (2 + h^2 (1 - m))) ||x_0 - x*||^2 with q = 2 m h^2 - 4 (1 + m) h + m + 7.
